Practical 1: Photoshop Basic Shapes

Name: Bhoomi Agarwal
Roll No.: 25260150
Course: Desktop Publishing – UAC012P

Objective

To learn how to create basic shapes in Adobe Photoshop.

Tools Used

* Rectangle Tool
* Ellipse Tool
* Polygon Tool
* Text Tool

Procedure

1. Open Adobe Photoshop.
2. Create a new document.
3. Draw a rectangle using the Rectangle Tool.
4. Draw a circle using the Ellipse Tool.
5. Draw a triangle using the Polygon Tool.
6. Create a pentagon using the Polygon Tool.
7. Apply different colors to the shapes.
8. Add headings and labels using the Text Tool.
9. Save the final design.

Result

Successfully created basic shapes using Adobe Photoshop.
